Chapter 10-34: "When the Time Comes"

—The truth is, what we know about the 'Beloved Children' is frustratingly little.

They are a group under the direct command of the Lust Sin Archbishop, Capella Emerada Lugnica, and apparently they themselves have no awareness of belonging to the Witch Cult—they see themselves purely as Capella's subordinates. Those currently carrying out the 'Body-Swapping Dolls' across the Kingdom of Lugnica are in a different position altogether; among Capella's subordinates, only a select few are counted as 'Beloved Children.'

And the condition for being chosen as one of those select 'Beloved Children' is—

"—Having a special power that no one else possesses. Mama... that person called it the children's 'talent.' Because a special person deserves special children..."

"The more I hear, the more it sounds like garbage logic, and the fact that it's so consistent with my understanding is terrifying. So, 'White Sheep'-chan, what's your basis for saying the 'Beloved Children' have arrived—and that there are two or more?"

"It's an inference from what's happening. The fact that we couldn't control our hearts, and the fact that sound disappeared... these are clearly occurring separately."

"Is there no chance it's one person with multiple powers—a multi-ability user?"

"I can't say absolutely not, but I think it's more likely that 'Beloved Children' don't act alone. —They're made to watch each other so they don't run away."

Even the answer to that question was smeared with Capella's vileness, making him feel sick.

But Subaru himself thought that possibility was low. After all, when it came to people with multiple abilities, the only ones who came to mind were Reinhardt and the Gluttony Sin Archbishop. Both were outliers—existences at the extremes of good and evil—and it was hard to imagine such people being common.

One ability per person—just as with Divine Protections and Authorities, he decided to keep that in mind for now.

"If that's the case, the question of what I am starts choking me, but never mind that. 'White Sheep'-chan, do you have any idea which 'Beloved Children' have arrived?"

"I'm sorry. Actually, even among 'Beloved Children,' we barely know each other... I only know one older woman who told me herself that she has a body that's very hard to kill."

"Hard to kill... well, that's certainly an ability of sorts. But for clues about the current situation... right!

If 'White Sheep'-chan is also a 'Beloved Child,' then you should have some kind of specialty too—"

"—!"

In front of Subaru, who had thought maybe there was a breakthrough there, 'White Sheep' caught her breath. Seeing her round eyes tremble and her cheeks stiffen, Subaru realized he had failed in his choice of topic.

She doesn't think well of her own ability. That was only natural. Because of that power, she was fixated upon by Capella, and even now she's forced into a position she doesn't want.

"Um, 'Grey Star'-san, I..."

"No, sorry, you don't have to say it if you don't want to. —There are still moves we can make."

Shaking his head at her hoarse voice, Subaru looked behind him at the corridor crushed into silence. Beyond that rubble should be Beatrice—they'd been separated from her and the others, but—

"Deep breath... and focus! —'Cor Leonis'!"

Exhaling the breath he'd taken largely, Subaru concentrated his awareness in his chest and activated the Authority of Greed—'Cor Leonis,' which locates allies and perceives their existence. Ideally, he'd be able to sense even Emilia and the others far away, but that was asking too much of Subaru's ability.

So for now, he'd settle for just the positions of allies within the Kugelschreiber Castle—

"—Beako and 'Black Dog' are together. Moving alone is Crusch-san, and the two together quite far away must be Russell-san and the others. The rest is..."

From the approximate distance and movement, and the color of the light he could sense as allies' presence, he could confirm the positional relationships and safety of Beatrice and the others within the castle.

And so, stacking up confirmations of each person's safety and relief one by one—he found it.

"—Ferris."

Separated from Subaru and everyone else, at a point where only one person had been isolated and pushed away, he definitely sensed Ferris's presence. It was a weak, frail light, but—

"There, there he is! It's Ferris! That guy—that guy's alive!"

"Eh, that's a really good thing, but how does 'Grey Star'-san know that...?"

"Actually, I have a sensor-like ability that lets me sense allies' positions! So when I tried to confirm everyone's location, Ferris was there too. That guy's safe... no, whether he's safe is questionable. The response is pretty weak. But he's alive. If he's alive... we can rendezvous!"

At that glimmer of hope, Subaru clenched his hands so hard his nails dug into his palms.

At the 'Return by Death' restart point, Ferris had already been taken away from Subaru's group in silence. In the worst case, the restart point itself might already have been too late.

That possibility always existed. And Subaru couldn't bear it.

"But it's not that. It's not that... Ferris is... below? Damn, I should've had Beako draw me a map of the castle! Anyway, I need to go save him right now—"

"Please calm down, 'Grey Star'-san! We can't do it alone!"

'White Sheep' spread both arms and blocked Subaru, who looked about to dash off at any moment toward Ferris's response, whose safety was in question. She looked straight at Subaru as he stumbled forward,

"I believe you're not lying. But please, calm down. Without 'Black Dog' or 'Emerald Beauty,' if we face the enemy, we'll just be defeated!"

"That's... yeah, damn, you're right! I got heated and couldn't see again...!"

'White Sheep' splashed water on Subaru's words as he fell into tunnel vision from impatience. His vision cleared, but the size of the problem hadn't changed. Only the order of dealing with it.

"'White Sheep'-chan, can you fight? I've got some cunning and a whip."

"I-I have some staff techniques and some magic."

"With this hand, fighting would be reckless... then let's join up with Beako and 'Black Dog,' who haven't moved from their spot. We won't be able to catch up to Crusch-san, who's fast on her feet."

"—Understood. Um, you can tell the location with your power, right, 'Grey Star'-san?"

"Yeah, let's go! I can't tell the path, but it's this way!"

Without disrupting his concentration, maintaining 'Cor Leonis,' he began running while leading 'White Sheep.'

Ferris's safety was still uncertain, but he had no choice but to believe this was the best option now. They'd rendezvous with Beatrice and the others as quickly as possible, heal 'Black Dog,' and head to rescue Ferris. If possible, he'd like to pick up Crusch and Russell and the others too, and have everyone go together.

Of course, if too many people clustered together, there was a risk they couldn't counter that phenomenon called emotional 'Collapse,' so whether that was truly the best option was questionable, but—

"—?"

As he ran thinking this, Subaru furrowed his brow at a sudden sense of unease.

Inside the unfamiliar castle, detouring around broken walls and corridors with missing floors, Subaru should be running the shortest possible route toward the light of Beatrice and the others he could sense. Of course, it was movement while staying alert, since encountering enemies along the way would be the worst.

But—

"Um, 'Grey Star'-san... there's something hard to say."

"...Don't say it. No, actually, please say it. I want to face reality too."

To 'White Sheep,' who brought it up hesitantly, Subaru ordered with a bitter expression.

Receiving that, 'White Sheep' looked around while slightly stiffening her body—

"—We've passed through here once already. We're going in circles around the same place."

"I knew it! I thought it was obvious too. That broken pillar, I saw it earlier."

Turning left at the T-junction at the dead end, a collapsed pillar blocked the corridor. There were many similar sights, but this was definitely the same one. —Because the distance to Beatrice, whom they should be heading straight toward, hadn't shrunk at all.

"Don't tell me, besides 'Silence' that erases sound and 'Collapse' that amplifies emotions, they can also make people 'Lost'? Don't tell me all the 'Beloved Children' are here...!"

It was a statement made on momentum, but since the Sin Archbishops had all gathered in Pristella before, it couldn't be dismissed as just a joke. But if that were the case, compared to then, their allies' fighting strength was far too weak. At least, he'd like to trade Rachins for Reinhardt.

"I'd also trade myself for Garfiel, and bring Julius and Roswaal too. Better yet, call Sechs as a reinforcement and flip the table—"

"I-I don't think all the 'Beloved Children' would be out... but if the enemy intends to settle things here, it's possible. Um, there's also the hidden door leading to the laboratory, so the possibility that we're being led astray by this castle's mechanisms isn't zero, but..."

"If that's the case, then Beako prioritizing reminiscing over castle security is too much of a Fielders' Choice. Also, there are two things bothering me. Both about Crusch-san."

Holding up two fingers, 'White Sheep' blinked, "Emerald Beauty-san?"

When he heard 'lost corridor,' the first thing Subaru remembered was the prank played on him by Beatrice at Roswaal's mansion—a corridor that looped infinitely. That was a kind of illusion, but Crusch's 'Dragon's Eye' should have seen through it at a glance.

In addition, after clashing with 'Black Dog' due to the discord brought by 'Collapse' and cutting him down, Crusch said she'd look for Ferris and ran off in her original direction. —That was also strange.

"If she's looking for Ferris, she should go back the way we came. He was taken by 'Silence' because he was walking at the very back... and indeed, I think Ferris is underground, in that direction."

It was hard to grasp the positional relationship precisely, but 'Cor Leonis' said Ferris's current location was underground, closer to the entrance than where Subaru and the others were, heading deeper into the castle.

Even Crusch, even with her blood up from 'Collapse,' should have understood that much.

"But she ran forward. There was nothing off about Crusch-san. If the same kind of thing is happening to us now..."

They think they're heading toward their destination, but they can't get any closer to it. —They're being messed with. Their sense of distance and direction. They're running on the rail next to the rail they think they're on.

Because of that, Subaru and the others—no, probably none of their allies will reach their destination.

"...Hey, this is quietly bad."

He'd inferred the opponent's abilities from what had happened, but each one individually didn't seem like much of a threat—yet depending on the situation and how they combined, they could pursue this level of harassment.

As expected of Capella's children—when it came to making people miserable, they were all stars.

"Ah, 'White Sheep'-chan is an exception, of course, separate. 'Black Dog' guy, I'm withholding judgment for now..."

"—Maybe we should reconsider our assumptions."

"Eh?"

"Even if we keep blindly trying to rendezvous, we definitely won't reach them. Somewhere along the way, we need to make our own move too... 'Grey Star'-san."

'White Sheep,' who had been thinking with her hand to her mouth, suddenly raised her head. When Subaru said "Yes!" in surprise at her vigor, she indicated the entire castle with both hands,

"You can sense allies' locations, right? Anyone's fine. Try pointing at them."

"—. Got it. That way, Beako is there. 'Black Dog' too."

Following 'White Sheep's' instruction, wondering if she had some idea, he pointed in the direction of the light he sensed. Confirming that direction, 'White Sheep' nodded "Understood," and then,

"Then let's try heading that way. Ready, set—"

"Wha—when you say it suddenly—huh?"

Urged on by 'White Sheep' without warning, Subaru hurriedly took a step. —In the opposite direction from where he was pointing, where Beatrice was.

At his own undoubtedly abnormal movement, he couldn't help but swallow.

"Don't tell me my brain's wiring is being messed with like this? If so..."

"—No, this time try closing your eyes. Then walk toward the direction where you sense 'Librarian'-san."

"—? My eyes? But I don't think that would change anything..."

Though he couldn't imagine it would, he closed his eyes and focused his awareness on 'Cor Leonis.' Still the same, he stepped toward Beatrice beside 'Black Dog' from the darkness behind his eyelids—

"—Just as I thought."

At 'White Sheep's' voice, he opened his eyes and confirmed his position.

He'd moved just one step, but that step, unlike the earlier one in the wrong direction, had properly advanced toward where he sensed Beatrice.

"W-What was different? Don't tell me it's a vision-based illusion..."

"Probably, 'Grey Star'-san's power output exceeded the current 'Lost.' The power relationships between Divine Protections, Demon Eyes, and abilities are extremely strict, so..."

"Ability... I see, because 'Cor Leonis' is an Authority."

If he could surpass the opponent through ability power relationships, then an Authority could overwrite the effects of the opponent's power.

If he closed his eyes and focused one hundred percent on 'Cor Leonis,' then the obstacle preventing him from reaching his destination due to 'Lost' could be broken through—

"Great achievement, 'White Sheep'-chan! This'll work! Alright, now follow me for real!"

"Ah, please wait! It seems like it'll work, but..."

"No, we've already lost a lot of time! We'll make it up from here—bnonorefuh!"

Following the breakthrough he'd finally found, Subaru tried to boldly chase Beatrice's light with his eyes closed—and his body slammed head-on into a hard wall, flipping dramatically into the corridor.

He hit his forehead and nose hard. When he flipped, he couldn't even break his fall.

"Gaaah... damn, of course... walls and pillars don't disappear..."

"S-Sorry, I couldn't make it in time!"

"N-No, it's not your fault. It's mine. My head's fault. ...But damn, what do we do?"

Even though they'd found a way to avoid being misled by 'Lost,' this being a ballpoint castle full of dead ends and detours hadn't changed. To avoid repeating the current tragedy, Subaru with his eyes closed would have to proceed cautiously, checking walls and floors—

"I might be able to guide you on the state of the path from behind, helping a little..."

"But that still means we'll be slow, huh. And thanks to all the getting lost, the distance to Beako and the others has grown. Getting there is..."

"—Is it not realistic right now?"

Nodding to 'White Sheep,' who had caught up with the conclusion of Subaru's train of thought.

Currently, the need to hurry and rendezvous with Beatrice and the others hadn't changed, but even using the method they'd found, they couldn't predict how long it would take to rendezvous.

And while doing so—

"—Crusch-san's movement changed. This is—she's fighting...!"

Crusch, who had been moving quickly through the castle, stopped and began movements other than running at that location. From the changes in the light and heat he could sense, Subaru felt the signs of her fighting. Moreover, he could even guess who she was fighting.

Because—

"It's not that far, yet I can't hear the sound of fighting."

Facing the direction where he sensed Crusch's presence, Subaru felt an overly quiet atmosphere, like the silence brought by a Japanese garden, coming from there. —Undoubtedly, Crusch was fighting 'Silence.'

Unconsciously, Subaru put his hand to his stomach, remembering the wide blade that had pierced him from behind. It wasn't hard to imagine that was 'Silence's' weapon.

"—"

In that instant, two thoughts sparked against each other in Subaru's mind.

If Crusch was fighting the enemy, the proper thought was that they should rush to her aid.

If the opponent was 'Silence,' the humiliating thought was that Subaru and the others' presence would be a hindrance.

"—With 'Silence' as the opponent, we can't coordinate either."

It would be different if they had a relationship where they could coordinate without words, in perfect sync, but unfortunately, Subaru and Crusch didn't have that kind of relationship, and their abilities weren't even on the same level to begin with.

Therefore, a careless rendezvous could itself be an act of aiding the enemy. —That's what made Subaru hesitate to join Crusch at this moment.

And there was one more reason Subaru thought this way—

"—From here, Ferris is close."

Yes, that's right. Within a realistic distance that Subaru, with his eyes closed, could reach using 'Cor Leonis' responses as a guide, both Crusch and Ferris were there.

Crusch was engaged with the enemy, and Ferris had either been captured or was injured and immobile, left behind. Either way, both were in different predicaments.

However, if there was something to consider, it was that 'Silence' wasn't currently by Ferris's side.

Now that 'Silence' was fully occupied with Crusch—

"And if Ferris is there, the safety of our allies goes up dramatically. If we can rendezvous with 'Black Dog,' he can return to the front lines immediately. So..."

"So you're saying we should go save 'Blue Snake'-san."

Receiving Subaru's theoretical armament, 'White Sheep' tightened her lips on her lovely face and pondered.

He understood her concern. No matter what, Subaru and 'White Sheep' were non-combatants, and even if they recklessly saved Ferris, it would just mean three non-combatants, far from a boost in fighting strength. Even without 'Silence,' the enemy still had at least 'Collapse' and 'Lost.' In the end, they hadn't found any real countermeasure against those.

If they wanted to avoid risk, they should aim to rendezvous with Beatrice and the others even if it took time.

"—But on a path that takes zero risks, you can't gain anything you want either."

"'Grey Star'-san..."

"Honestly, I'm aware I'm asking for something pretty difficult. 'White Sheep'-chan has her own reasons for being in 'Six Tongues,' things she has to accomplish. I'm sure you can't afford to fail, right? But... but!"

If you fear failure and hesitate, you won't be able to step forward even at the crucial moment.

Subaru had learned that through countless failures, and each time, he'd been struck down by regret and frustration that felt like his soul being torn apart.

Because he was that kind of person, he could say it. —The time will definitely come.

"Let's show our spirit here. So we can face our precious comrades with pride."

"—I..."

He didn't know if this was the best choice. Whether it was a choice worth dragging people into the same fire.

But he knew that if he didn't choose this here, he would regret it to death.

And to Subaru's words, 'White Sheep' nodded back with a determined expression—

"I'll choose too. —So that I can face that person with pride."

△▼△▼△▼△

—Always, always always, always always always, he thinks.

Why am I so useless? Why am I so pathetic? Why am I so defective?

The voice tormenting himself with "why" never disappears. —That too was a kind of self-pleasure.

"Really, I hate myself..."

The moment he woke up and understood his situation, he wanted to die of shame. Of course, he couldn't die that way. By any method, this life couldn't be easily taken.

That was Felix Argyle's specialty—so miserable it made him want to curse.

"—Hey, I'm always, always thinking about this, will you listen?"

Suddenly, while he was cursing himself, such a high-pitched voice came from directly in front of him. Glancing over, standing there was a woman with long hair wearing a black hat and black dress.

She put both hands together in front of her face, looked at Felix with dreamy eyes,

"Don't you think the right hand and left hand were born to nestle together like this for their whole lives—like fated existences? The right foot and left foot are different. Because they never stick together like this, right? So feet don't love each other... but the right hand and left hand!"

"—"

"No, wait a moment? If you look more closely, it's not just hands—fingers overlap perfectly too, right? Thumb, index finger, middle finger! And the pinky! It's still a pinky!"

The woman, blushing, writhed and squealed with delight at whatever was so fun about this. Her attitude was so irritating that he wanted to throw cold water on it.

"...Some people are born without one hand. There are people who lose hands or fingers to injury too."

"—"

It was an extreme argument, but the one who'd thrown out an extreme argument that was already dead to begin with was the woman.

Maybe he'd touch a nerve and get hurt. Even if that happened, he had a somewhat desperate feeling that it would be fine if he could get her attention.

However—

"...That's the best."

Far from getting angry, the woman exhaled feverishly with ecstasy, her eyes moist as she looked at Felix. Then she raised both hands above her head and began spinning in place,

"Because love burns brighter the higher the obstacle! Class differences! Race differences! Age, gender, ethics, morality, law! All of it, all of it is fuel to make love burn brighter! And what's the greatest obstacle... fufu, ufufu, do・you・know?"

"—"

He regretted throwing cold water instantly.

It was a vein that yielded nothing worthwhile no matter how deep you dug. Or perhaps he'd struck a spring that only gushed poison. —Actually, the word poison wasn't far off.

"...You've been doing something to me all along, haven't you? What is this?"

"Something... you mean your arm? If that's it, that wasn't me—Reborn did that. Really, what a brute. For a brute like Reborn, I think someone older, generous and composed, or conversely someone younger who needs more care, would suit him! How about it!?"

"Not the arm. You're trying to mess with my head."

"Ah, that one? Fufu, don't misunderstand. I'm not doing that just to you. To everyone in this castle... ah! Could it be you wanted to be special, just you? But if so, does that mean you like me? Me too!"

To the woman who proclaimed love with dreamy eyes, Felix abandoned hope for a proper conversation.

Even without that, no fool would reveal their hand to the enemy. As a matter of fact, Felix felt external interference on his body and his body continuously healing from it.

The special technique woven into Felix's body was a continuously active magic that kept his body in optimal condition at all times. With this, Felix could respond to abnormalities through changes in his body and Od, even if he didn't notice them, and recover.

Even now, he was continuously healing the strange power the woman was apparently imposing on him.

However, this power had a flaw. —Felix's own physical fragility.

"—"

Ignoring the writhing woman, the surroundings—it seemed to indeed be inside Kugelschreiber Castle, but it was an unfamiliar space. It looked like a landing typical of castles and mansions, but the high walls had no windows at all. Probably underground.

In that underground, Felix was a prisoner. —With both arms raised above his head, literally skewered, pinned to the wall.

"Frustrating, but a hundred-point finishing move..."

As mentioned, Felix's body continuously recovered to perfect condition, but with his body pierced by a blade, there was no way to heal the wound without dealing with the blade.

And Felix, hung with his arms skewered, didn't have the physical ability to pull it out and gain freedom.

Because of that, he could only continue in this spectacle-like state—

"Don't make that face, Felix. It ruins your cute face, you know? Besides, besides? I think this isn't a bad deal for you either."

"Huh? Why?"

"Actually, right now it's in a state where people have a really hard time getting here! Everyone has to take a 'Detour,' and some people get discouraged or cry along the way. But but, if someone overcomes that obstacle and reaches here... that's your fated partner! This 'Ring Finger' Lycoris guarantees it! Burning love will envelop you!"

Because he'd reflexively responded to a conversation he had no intention of having, he ended up listening to worthless delusions droning on, and the only thing he gained was the woman's name—Lycoris.

On top of that, what Lycoris called hope was unmistakably Felix's despair.

"...A knight as a hostage, the worst."

Even if he had no knightly prowess and it was just an ornamental title, an existence that should be protected waiting for someone's salvation was nothing but a nightmare. Especially if it would result in dragging down the person he absolutely didn't want to drag down.

And for Felix, the most unbearable thing was—

"—If it were Reinhardt coming, I wouldn't mind at all."

He'd have loved to say it in a dying voice, but Felix's throat and tongue were in perfect condition, so it didn't come out that way. Because he'd made the magic that way himself.

Whether she knew this or not, the other party let out a small "ha" like exhaling, and laughed,

"You look way more alive than you seem, Ferris."

Deliberately or perhaps just excited, a boy with glittering eyes appeared in the landing almost dancing, making his footsteps ring unnecessarily loud. Looking at Felix, pinned to the farthest wall of the wide space, from the underground entrance, the boy—Natsuki Subaru—glared at Lycoris standing at the feet of the hanging Felix.

And with sharp eyes still, he pointed at her dramatically,

"Hyahha! Finally we meet, 'Beloved Children'! I've been waiting impatiently for the day I could see your faces!"

"—"

At Subaru, who widened his eyes and shouted with a booming voice cracked with vigor, Felix furrowed his brow. Even for his usual bravado, it was a bit much.

"...So this is that kind of thing."

If what was happening to Subaru now was caused by the same factor as what Felix's body kept healing, he could guess what Lycoris was doing.

She was scattering it. —A 'poison' in the air that drives people mad.

Lycoris, displaying her literally poisonous woman nature, hugged herself as if terrified by Subaru's outburst,

"Just as I thought! Just as I thought! Natsuki loved Felix! Otherwise he couldn't have crossed Tornell's 'Detour' to get here! Just as I thought, just as I hoped, just as I wished, just as I dreamed, just as just as just as just as precious—!!"

Stampeding in place, Lycoris writhed with joy beyond limits.

Subaru, seeing it for the first time, didn't hide his revulsion and readied his whip. He seemed prepared to fight Lycoris, but—

"...Where's Beatrice-chan?"

"I'm operating separately from Beako! And it's not just Beako! But don't worry, you're not alone! Me neither! I have reliable comrades! First, the whip!"

"The whip! What are you going to use it for!? Is that love too!? Can I watch from the side? Or should I join in? Is that love? If it's love, I don't mind joining!"

"Also courage! When it comes down to it, this is what I rely on! And, the trump card too—"

He probably wanted to say there was one.

In the nightmare-like scene of Subaru and Lycoris making a racket together, Felix even felt doubtful whether this was reality.

That's why. —He couldn't catch up with what happened the next moment.

"—If the trump card is me, then I'm sorry."

Suddenly, a figure appeared behind Subaru, who was shouting loudly, and clung to his body. —No, wrong. It only looked like clinging. The reality was different. She'd slammed into him with her whole body.

Why? Because that way, it wouldn't come off. Because it would sink in deep. —Because the sharp knife she held at waist level with both hands could skillfully gouge Subaru's vital spot in his side.

"Shiro, hitsuji, chan...?"

Seeing the knife stuck in his side and the person gripping it, Subaru called that name, that nickname. Neither Subaru nor Felix knew her real name.

"Buh," Subaru spilled overflowing blood from his mouth and fell to his knees. At Subaru on his knees, she—'White Sheep'—looked down with eyes colder than anything they'd ever seen, and said:

"—I chose. To fulfill my own wish as well."
